{
  "version": 1,
  "nav_cycle": null,
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Point Merge",
    "note": "Oslo Gardermoen's Point Merge System for runway 01L: arrivals on the ADOPI 3L, BELGU 3L and RIPAM 3L routes, each route's aircraft at least 120 s in trail. The controller turns each aircraft direct to the merge point, VALPU, from its sequencing leg, and may hold or reduce its speed, never below 200 KT, the speed every aircraft crosses VALPU at. Past VALPU the aircraft flies the approach as background traffic. Each aircraft is scored on its time behind the previous one over VALPU, its flight time and the reductions it needed, with a cost for every second in loss of separation; the reward is shaped by the conflicts BlueSky predicts within 5 minutes (PBRS). Each aircraft observes its own and every intruder's time to VALPU along their routes."
  },
